<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Manrique Pérez de Lara</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1164">1164</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Manrique Pérez de Lara was a Castilian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnates">magnate</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-lara">House of Lara</a> and the first lord of Molina. He held Molina under Castilian overlordship and in 1154 granted it a fuero, a charter of rights for settlers. After the death of Sancho III he acted as regent for the young <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-viii">Alfonso VIII</a> and was killed at the Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huete">Huete</a> in 1164.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/manrique-perez-de-lara.jpg" alt="Manrique Pérez de Lara" width="320" height="179" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alfonso_VII_charter_1156b.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
